 |  Data (observed vector time-series)
 |  ----------------------------------
 |
 |  VTS : pandas.DataFrame,
 |          index (ts_list), columns (asof_list)
 |      Observed vector time-series, as input data
 |          for dAeDFM model learning and inference
 |      Row time-series of column vector with first
 |          column as oldest and last one as latest
 |
 |  ts_list : list
 |      List of name/symbol/label strings of
 |          observed time-series, as list of
 |          index axis of VTS DataFrame
 |
 |  asof_list : list
 |      List of as-of time-stamps, here, of
 |          observed vector time-series data,
 |          as list of columns axis of VTS
 |          DataFrame
 |
 |  num_ts : int >= 1
 |      Number of observed time-series
 |          = len(ts_list)
 |
 |  len_ts : int > 1
 |      Length of observed vector time-series
 |          = len(asof_list)
 |      Note: len_ts >= len_learn_window + (2 var_order)
 |
 |  Parameters (dynamic factor model)
 |  ---------------------------------
 |
 |  len_learn_window : int, >> 1
 |      Length of trailing time window of data points
 |          for model learning
 |
 |  var_order : int, >= 1
 |      Vector autoregressive (VAR) order, p, of dynamic
 |          factor model of vector time-series
 |      Notes:
 |          var_order <= len_learn_window
 |          len_ts >= len_learn_window + (2 var_order)
 |
 |  max_forecast_step : int >= 1
 |      Maximum number of forecasting steps of time-series
 |          forecasts
 |
 |  target_type_list : list, ['s', 'S', 'standardized',
 |          'b', 'B', 'base-case', 'z', 'Z', 'zero-mean',
 |          'o', 'O', 'original']
 |      List of valid values of target_type
 |
 |  target_type : str, (in target_type_list)
 |      Specified type of vector, or multiple, time-series
 |          data on which model inferences, predictions or
 |          forecasts are made, and are evaluated
 |      Type 's', 'S', 'standardized', 'b', 'B', 'base-case':
 |          Inferences/forecasts are made/evaluated on
 |          standardized, or base-case, values of observed
 |          vector time-series
 |      Type 'z', 'Z', 'zero-mean':
 |          Inferences/forecasts are made/evaluated on zero-
 |          mean, or de-meaned, values of observed vector
 |          time-series
 |      Type 'o', 'O', 'original':
 |          Inferences/forecasts are made/evaluated on values
 |          of original/observed vector time-series
 |
 |  fwd_cumsum : bool (True, or False)
 |      Whether or not to make cum-sum forecast
 |      Notes: for base-case, fwd_cumsum = False
 |
 |  Parameters (deep autoencoder)
 |  -----------------------------
 |
 |  num_ts_input : int, num_ts
 |      Number of time-series in observed vector
 |      time-series
 |
 |  data_layer_id : int = 0
 |      ID label of layer containing input data vector
 |          of deep autoencoder
 |
 |  num_latent_layer : int >= 2
 |      Number of latent layers in deep autoencoder
 |          for nonlinear dynamic factor model
 |
 |  dae_layer_list : int,
 |          [0, 1, 2, ..., num_latent_layer]
 |      List of ID labels of data and latent layers for
 |          encoding, decoding and output
 |
 |  num_ts_dict : dict, keys (dae_layer_list)
 |          obj[key] : int
 |      Number of (observed or letant) time-seres
 |          at specified layers in deep autoencoder
 |      Notes: num_ts_input = num_ts_dict[0]
 |          > num_ts_dict[1] > num_ts_dict[2] > ...
 |          > num_ts_dict[num_latent_layer]
 |
 |  num_ts_latent : int >= 1,
 |          = num_ts_dict[num_latent_layer]
 |      Number of latent time-series at hidden
 |          bottleneck layer
 |
 |  num_ts_output : int, num_ts
 |      Number of time-series in observed vector
 |      time-series
 |
 |  encoding_layer_list : list, [...,
 |          '(num_ts_dict[i],num_ts_dict[i+1])', ...]
 |      List of ID strings of encoding layers
 |      Notes: of specified encoding layer,
 |          in_featurs = num_ts_dict[i] * var_order
 |          out_featurs = num_ts_dict[i+1] * var_order
 |      Notes: i = 0, 1, ..., (num_latent_layer - 1)
 |
 |  decoding_layer_list : list, [...,
 |          '(num_ts_dict[i],num_ts_dict[i-1])', ...]
 |      List of ID strings of decoding layers
 |      Notes: of specified decoding layer,
 |          in_featurs = num_ts_dict[i] * var_order
 |          out_featurs = num_ts_dict[i-1] * var_order
 |      Notes: i = num_latent_layer, (num_latent_layer - 1),
 |          ..., 2
 |
 |  dae_layer_spec : dict, keys (
 |              encoding_layer_list + decoding_layer_list)
 |          obj[key] : str, in ['nowcast',
 |              'n', 'N', 'forecast', 'f', F']
 |      Nowcasting/forecasting specification
 |          of each of all encoding and decoding
 |          layers of deep autoencoder
 |      Notes on models
 |          (1) Total nowcasting
 |              all encoding/decoding layers 'N'
 |          (2) Predictive nowcasting
 |              first encoding layer 'N', some other 'F'
 |          (3) One-step forecasting
 |              first encoding layer 'F', all others 'N'
 |          (4) Enhanced forecasting
 |              first encoding layer 'F', others 'F'/'N'
 |          (5) Total forecasting
 |              all encoding/decoding layers 'F'
 |
 |  causal_layer_ratio : float, 0 <= ratio <= 1
 |      Weight of causal (nowcasting/forecasting) sub-
 |          layer output in total nonlinear layer output
 |          (from all causal and dense sub-layers)
 |      Notes: bottlelneck encoding and output
 |          decoding layer, always dense linear
 |      Notes: this ratio to be treated
 |          as 0 if < 0.05, and as 1 if > 0.95
 |
 |  init_pcwt_ratio : float, 0 <= ratio <= 1
 |      Portion of PCA-based initial weight values
 |          in total initial random weight values
 |          of linear layers of deep autoencoder
 |
 |  Parameters (model training)
 |  ---------------------------
 |
 |  num_epoch : int
 |      Number of iterations taking entire input
 |          datasets to train deep autoencoder
 |
 |  patience : int > 1
 |      Number of training epochs to run without
 |          validation metric improvement before
 |          early stopping
 |
 |  batch_size : int, < len_learn_window
 |      Size of mini-batches for mini-batch
 |          gradient descent
 |
 |  train_criterion : dict, keys ('grad', 'stats')
 |          obj['grad'] : str, in [
 |              'SquaredL1Loss', 'SmoothL1Loss',
 |              'HuberLoss', 'MSELoss']
 |          obj['stats'] : str,
